{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgELSFLWGXotEtpSwoSwV", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01RCeAkbKNhNnS2kme47bBzG", "name": "WebSearch", "input": {"query": "Korean pouch origin Neolithic tied to waist carry stone axe knives hunting cooking tools", "mode": "standard"}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1552, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5672, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1552}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T23:12:31.056Z", "request_id": "req_011CgELSF2uYEc7GXkBY2E8K", "wire_tool_inputs": {"toolu_01RCeAkbKNhNnS2kme47bBzG": {"query": "Korean pouch origin Neolithic tied to waist carry stone axe knives hunting cooking tools", "mode": "standard"}}}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01RCeAkbKNhNnS2kme47bBzG", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://www.rrncommunity.org/items/30432\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.rrncommunity.org/items/30404/print\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.rrncommunity.org/items/30432/print\"}, {\"url\": \"https://rrncommunity.org/items/30219/print\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.rrncommunity.org/items/3397\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.rrncommunity.org/items/2967/print\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.rrncommunity.org/items/30433\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.rrncommunity.org/items/2967\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.rrncommunity.org/items/30404\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T23:12:36.909Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Korean pouch origin Neolithic tied to waist carry stone axe knives hunting cooking tools", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_014cHFqx7SDowGcDhTCHR6i6", "content": [{"title": "www.rrncommunity.org", "url": "https://www.rrncommunity.org/items/30432"}, {"title": "Waist Bag Item Number: N3.34 from the MOA: University of British Columbia", "url": "https://www.rrncommunity.org/items/30404/print"}, {"title": "Waist Bag Item Number: N3.36 from the MOA: University of British Columbia", "url": "https://www.rrncommunity.org/items/30432/print"}, {"title": "Waist Bag Item Number: N3.2 from the MOA: University of British Columbia", "url": "https://rrncommunity.org/items/30219/print"}, {"title": "www.rrncommunity.org", "url": "https://www.rrncommunity.org/items/3397"}, {"title": "Waist Bag Item Number: N3.3 from the MOA: University of British Columbia", "url": "https://www.rrncommunity.org/items/2967/print"}, {"title": "www.rrncommunity.org", "url": "https://www.rrncommunity.org/items/30433"}, {"title": "www.rrncommunity.org", "url": "https://www.rrncommunity.org/items/2967"}, {"title": "www.rrncommunity.org", "url": "https://www.rrncommunity.org/items/30404"}]}, "The search didn't turn up anything on a Neolithic origin for Korean pouches, or on stone axes, knives, hunting, or cooking tools. The results are all from museum-style catalog entries about later waist bags, so the Neolithic link in the query is unconfirmed.\n\nWhat the results do cover is the later waist bag. These pouches were hung from the waist ties of skirts or trousers to hold small items, since clothing lacked pockets until Western influence arrived. Before western influences reached Korea, clothing did not have pockets, and such waist bags \"gui-jo-mo-ni\" were used to carry small articles. Their function was mostly ornamental. As they hung outside their clothes, they looked colourful and pretty, and their functions were more decorative than practical. Use declined after the opening of Korea to the outside world in the late 19th century.\n\nFor the origin question, you'd likely need archaeological or ethnographic sources on Neolithic Korean bone, stone, or fiber carrying containers, or on prehistoric tool kits, which these results don't address. A search for Korean Neolithic material culture or prehistoric bags or pouches may be more productive."], "durationSeconds": 5.784163499999999, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01RCeAkbKNhNnS2kme47bBzG", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_011dxKrHbak7cxrMZi98L8R2", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://calendar.prattlibrary.org/event/make-your-own-korean-lucky-pouch-orl\"}, {\"url\": \"https://scholar.kyobobook.co.kr/article/detail/4010024880340\"}, {\"url\": \"https://scholar.kyobobook.co.kr/article/detail/4010022817979\"}, {\"url\": \"https://scholar.kyobobook.co.kr/article/detail/4010024970814\"}, {\"url\": \"https://collections.vam.ac.uk/item/O22293\"}, {\"url\": \"https://scholarspace.manoa.hawaii.edu/items/55018e86-7863-465e-b264-5d938917c09f/full\"}, {\"url\": \"https://sozai.app/transcript/free-lecture-korean-history-prehistory-theory/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://steemit.steemapps.com/korea/@explore56/culture-of-korea\"}, {\"url\": \"https://sozai.app/transcript/free-lecture-korean-history-prehistory-theory/index.md\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T23:12:38.243Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "주머니 기원 신석기 시대 돌도끼 칼 사냥 조리 도구 허리에 묶어 한국 수공예", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01Lt39rViZkwSY5G8YMLTrnx", "content": [{"title": "make your own korean lucky pouch orl", "url": "https://calendar.prattlibrary.org/event/make-your-own-korean-lucky-pouch-orl"}, {"title": "scholar.kyobobook.co.kr", "url": "https://scholar.kyobobook.co.kr/article/detail/4010024880340"}, {"title": "scholar.kyobobook.co.kr", "url": "https://scholar.kyobobook.co.kr/article/detail/4010022817979"}, {"title": "scholar.kyobobook.co.kr", "url": "https://scholar.kyobobook.co.kr/article/detail/4010024970814"}, {"title": "collections.vam.ac.uk", "url": "https://collections.vam.ac.uk/item/O22293"}, {"title": "Craft Production and Social Change in Mumun Pottery Period Korea", "url": "https://scholarspace.manoa.hawaii.edu/items/55018e86-7863-465e-b264-5d938917c09f/full"}, {"title": "무료강의 공시한국사-[핵심이론 1.선사 시대 ] — Transcript", "url": "https://sozai.app/transcript/free-lecture-korean-history-prehistory-theory/"}, {"title": "한국의 문화[Culture of Korea.]", "url": "https://steemit.steemapps.com/korea/@explore56/culture-of-korea"}, {"title": "**무료강의 공시한국사-[핵심이론 1.선사 시대 ] — Transcript & Summary | SozAI**", "url": "https://sozai.app/transcript/free-lecture-korean-history-prehistory-theory/index.md"}]}, "검색 결과에서는 신석기 시대 주머니의 기원이나 돌도끼·칼·사냥·조리 도구를 허리에 묶어 쓴 사례를 직접 다룬 자료를 찾지 못했습니다. 관련성이 있는 내용만 정리하면 다음과 같습니다.\n\n- **한복과 주머니:** V&A 박물관 자료는 한복에 주머니가 없어서 지갑 형태의 장식 주머니가 장식과 실용을 겸했다고 설명합니다. 이 자료는 조선 후기 자수 주머니를 다루며, 신석기 시대는 다루지 않습니다. (Traditional Korean dress, hanbok, does not have pockets and a purse such as this one was both ornamental and functional.)\n- **신석기 시대 생활상:** 신석기 시대에는 간석기와 토기가 쓰이기 시작했고 원시 수공업이 발전했다는 개괄적 설명이 있습니다. 다만 주머니나 허리에 차는 도구에 대한 언급은 없습니다. (출처: sozai.app 강의 요약, index 9-3)\n- **신석기 장신구:** 패천(패류로 만든 장신구)과 팔찌 등 신석기 장신구 연구가 있으나, 착용 방식과 용도는 아직 명확하지 않다고 합니다. (출처: scholar.kyobobook.co.kr, index 3-2 및 3-5)\n\n신석기 시대 주머니의 기원을 알려면 \"한국 선사시대 주머니\", \"패천 용도\", \"신석기 가죽 끈 도구\" 등 더 구체적인 검색어로 다시 찾아보시는 것이 좋겠습니다. 현재 결과만으로는 질문의 핵심 주장(돌도끼·칼·조리 도구를 허리에 묶음)을 뒷받침할 근거가 없습니다."], "durationSeconds": 7.355168834, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_011dxKrHbak7cxrMZi98L8R2", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
