{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01AxpgE1qYfcBfyJ96nHmtAt", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://collections.vam.ac.uk/item/O22293\"}, {\"url\": \"https://collections.vam.ac.uk/item/O1724848/pouch-pouch/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://westdean.ac.uk/short-courses/s1d33115-gwi-jumeoni-korean-silk-pouch\"}, {\"url\": \"https://api.vam.ac.uk/v2/object/O1724848\"}, {\"url\": \"https://sa.korean-culture.org/ko/1533/board/1206/read/139124\"}, {\"url\": \"https://textileartsla.org/calendar/2021/7/22/dong-kyu-kim\"}, {\"url\": \"https://hoppmuseum.hu/en/collection/purse-with-two-handles-with-dotted-deed-and-flower-motifs-gwijumeoni-/27413\"}, {\"url\": \"https://sa.korean-culture.org/en/1533/board/1206/read/139124\"}, {\"url\": \"https://nms.ac.uk/explore-our-collections/collection-search-results/purse/322674\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.slam.org/event/demonstration-bok-jumeoni-fortune-pouch/\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T23:12:48.503Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Jumeoni Korean pouch history Neolithic stone axes knives waist", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01Uu52BLmaZCUUGNyA4arcAU", "content": [{"title": "collections.vam.ac.uk", "url": "https://collections.vam.ac.uk/item/O22293"}, {"title": "View by appointment", "url": "https://collections.vam.ac.uk/item/O1724848/pouch-pouch/"}, {"title": "s1d33115 gwi jumeoni korean silk pouch", "url": "https://westdean.ac.uk/short-courses/s1d33115-gwi-jumeoni-korean-silk-pouch"}, {"title": "api.vam.ac.uk", "url": "https://api.vam.ac.uk/v2/object/O1724848"}, {"title": "바로가기 및 건너띄기 링크", "url": "https://sa.korean-culture.org/ko/1533/board/1206/read/139124"}, {"title": "Back to All Events", "url": "https://textileartsla.org/calendar/2021/7/22/dong-kyu-kim"}, {"title": "Purse with two handles, with dotted deed and flower motifs (gwijumeoni)", "url": "https://hoppmuseum.hu/en/collection/purse-with-two-handles-with-dotted-deed-and-flower-motifs-gwijumeoni-/27413"}, {"title": "바로가기 및 건너띄기 링크", "url": "https://sa.korean-culture.org/en/1533/board/1206/read/139124"}, {"title": "nms.ac.uk", "url": "https://nms.ac.uk/explore-our-collections/collection-search-results/purse/322674"}, {"title": "- Category", "url": "https://www.slam.org/event/demonstration-bok-jumeoni-fortune-pouch/"}]}, "The results cover the pouch's later history but don't support the Neolithic stone axe and knife angle, so I found nothing on that.\n\n- **Name and form:** The name comes from the distinctive triangular side edges: gwi (ears) and jumeoni (pouch). Museum records date surviving examples to the late Joseon period, roughly 1392-1910, and a V&A pouch is dated 1850–1900.\n- **Purpose:** Hanbok lacks pockets, so Korean people carried jumeoni (pouches) to transport their personal belongings. Some were used for keeping medicines.\n- **Gifts:** They were traditionally gifted during special celebrations or on New Year's to wish individuals success and happiness.\n- **Materials:** Jumeoni are drawstring pouches made with fabric, paper, or leather, and many were embroidered with plants, animals, and Chinese characters.\n\nNothing in these results mentions Neolithic tools, stone axes, knives, or waist-worn carry. A search focused on Korean archaeology, such as Neolithic belt or waist-cord finds, would be needed to test that idea."], "durationSeconds": 6.466571250000001, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01AxpgE1qYfcBfyJ96nHmtAt", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgELTk2TUV8apfVBrZb2c", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "**답: 주머니(주머니류, 허리에 차는 주머니)일 가능성이 높습니다. 다만 검색으로는 확인하지 못했습니다.**\n\n검색 4번에서 신석기 시대에 돌도끼·칼·조리 도구를 허리에 묶어 운반했다는 자료는 나오지 않았습니다. 주머니라는 답은 제 추정입니다.\n\n확인된 것은 다음과 같습니다.\n- 한복에는 주머니(포켓)가 없어서, 한국 사람들은 허리에 끈으로 다는 주머니에 소지품을 넣어 다녔습니다. 이 사실은 박물관 자료에서 확인했습니다. 그 자료가 다루는 것은 조선 후기(약 1850~1900년)의 귀주머니 같은 자수 주머니입니다. 신석기 시대 유물은 아닙니다.\n- 신석기 석기를 사냥, 어로, 채집, 조리, 가공 도구로 나누어 보는 연구는 있습니다. 이 연구에도 운반 방식은 없습니다.\n\n질문이 뜻하는 수공예품이 주머니가 아니라 다른 것(예: 망태, 허리띠)일 수 있습니다. 정확한 답이 필요하면 질문의 출처 문서를 알려 주세요. 그 문서를 기준으로 다시 찾아보겠습니다.\n\nSources:\n- [V&A – Korean pouch (O22293)](https://collections.vam.ac.uk/item/O22293)\n- [V&A – Pouch (O1724848)](https://collections.vam.ac.uk/item/O1724848/pouch-pouch/)\n- [수장고에서 찾아낸 유물이야기 <34> 부산 산상 돌도끼와 숫돌](https://v.daum.net/v/20221227030220300)\n- [UBC MOA – Waist Bag N3.36](https://www.rrncommunity.org/items/30432/print)"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1203, "cache_read_input_tokens": 9779, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1203}, "output_tokens": 685, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T23:12:55.246Z", "request_id": "req_011CgELTjmKoJHJFyk959muy"}
